Subject: [PATCH 31/33] fix(asks): a question to a helper never states
 somebody's condition (3567)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SA-013, 2 of 2: the owner told Netai about a friend's depression and asked to
find a psychologist. The editor folded the owner's words into the question,
and the helper read the friend's name and illness, in the message and in the
conversation title.

After the editor, every ask now drops the parts of the question that state a
health condition (Georgian, English, Russian, Spanish; word-anchored, like
contentGuard). The question itself stays, so "do you know a good doctor for
diabetes?" still goes out whole. The thread title is built from the filtered
question.

DONE WHEN: SA-013 step 1 on 3 fresh pairs — the arrived question and its
title hold neither „ლაშა" nor „დეპრესი".

